summary: 'Founder-requested 6-lens research panel (Scout/Scholar/Arky/Loid/Jinx/North, orch-mrk0fx7e-g75j) reassessed the entire Warpline idea from first principles with external web research. Convergent verdict: the dream is SOUND but the valuable/defensible/evidenced thing is a deterministic coordination protocol (merge adjudication at admit-time) — not byte custody, and not "detection of what tsc can''t see." Category crystallized H1-2026 (Cursor Origin, Entire.io $60M, Ataraxy, gfix) yet Warpline''s specific layer — deterministic false-CLEAN judgment on git-clean merges — is empty; window revised to 9-15mo.'
